# Copy to .env.local and fill in to use real Postgres / S3-compatible storage (docker-compose.yml or a
# real cloud instance). Leave both unset to use the zero-install local fallback (PGlite + local
# filesystem storage) — see ADR-007. Next.js loads .env.local automatically; nothing else needed.

# --- Database (packages/db) ---
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://av_inspection:dev_only_password@localhost:5432/av_inspection_tours

# --- Object storage (packages/storage) ---
# S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
# S3_REGION=us-east-1
# S3_BUCKET=av-inspection-tours
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=av_inspection
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=dev_only_password
# S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true    # required for MinIO

# --- Microsoft 365 / SharePoint object storage (packages/storage/src/ms-graph-storage.ts) ---
# This is now the intended PERMANENT store for photos/audio/reports/attachments (S3/R2 above stays only as
# the local-dev fallback, unchanged) -- getStorage() picks MsGraphStorage over S3Storage when
# MS_GRAPH_TENANT_ID is set, regardless of whether S3_ENDPOINT is also set. Requires a one-time Entra ID
# admin setup first -- see the full numbered steps in packages/storage/src/graph-auth.ts's top comment
# (app registration, Sites.Selected admin consent, AND granting that app access to this specific site via
# the site's own /permissions endpoint -- all three are required, not just the first two).
# MS_GRAPH_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# MS_GRAPH_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# MS_GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET=dev_only_placeholder
#
# Identify the target SharePoint site EITHER by its already-resolved Graph site id (preferred -- one fewer
# lookup call per cold start; get this id once via the GET call documented in graph-auth.ts step 4)...
# MS_GRAPH_SITE_ID=contoso.sharepoint.com,11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111,22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
# ...OR by hostname + server-relative path, if that's easier to grab from the site's own URL bar:
# MS_GRAPH_SITE_HOSTNAME=contoso.sharepoint.com
# MS_GRAPH_SITE_PATH=/sites/AVInspectionTours
#
# MS_GRAPH_DRIVE_NAME=Documents               # the document library's display name (a site can have more than one)
# MS_GRAPH_ROOT_FOLDER=סיורי פיקוח             # configurable base folder inside that library -- not hardcoded

# --- PDF generation engine (apps/web/app/api/report/docx-to-pdf/route.ts) ---
# Default (this var unset, or anything other than "libreoffice"): the pure-JS engine
# (packages/report-generator/src/build-pdf.ts) -- no LibreOffice/Adobe/MS Office install needed at all,
# per the company's hard requirement. Set PDF_ENGINE=libreoffice ONLY to fall back to the old
# soffice-based conversion path (kept as an explicit, opt-in safety net during rollout -- see that
# route's own top comment for why).
# PDF_ENGINE=libreoffice

# --- Cloudflare Containers production deploy (see CLOUDFLARE_DEPLOY.md) ---
# These are NOT read from this file in production -- they're set as real Worker secrets/vars via
# `wrangler secret put` / wrangler.toml's [vars], then forwarded into the container by worker/index.ts.
# Listed here only as a reference for which values to gather before deploying:
#   DATABASE_URL        -> a real external Postgres (e.g. Neon free tier) -- Cloudflare has no
#                          first-party managed Postgres; local dev's PGlite fallback is dev-only.
#   S3_ENDPOINT         -> https://<account_id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com  (R2 is S3-API-compatible;
#                          the existing packages/storage/src/s3-storage.ts needs no code changes)
#   S3_BUCKET           -> your R2 bucket name
#   S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID / S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY -> an R2 API token (dashboard: R2 -> Manage API Tokens)
#   SOFFICE_PATH        -> already set to /usr/bin/soffice inside the Dockerfile -- don't override.
#                          Only read at all when PDF_ENGINE=libreoffice is also set (see above); the
#                          default pure-JS PDF engine ignores it entirely.
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY   -> only needed once the paused AI pipeline (Phase 6) is resumed
